{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me","id":102106,"title":"Explain the Dragonblooded Design Paradigm to me","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-30T12:37:10-07:00","id":102106,"title":"Explain the Dragonblooded Design Paradigm to me","content":"I've been reflecting lately on a somewhat unsatisfactory experience of playing a DB, and realized that I really don't get what DBs are really about.<br /> <br /> They're a type of Ability exalted, similar to Solars, but their Abilities are tied to their Aspects through what seems to be mostly thought-association rather than caste-role. Sometimes the association makes sense (Air=flying, flying=Throwing. OK!), and sometimes it doesn't (Arrow shafts are made of Wood. Wood=Archery?), and sometimes it seems to be based more on some kind of idea of Humorism (Fire= choleric, choleric = Presence?).<br /> <br /> The Aspect of each Dragonblood is not especially important except for the Anima power and class abilities, because every DB can use charms from the entire DB charmset, including those that are not of their element. For example, a Water-Aspect who wants to get good at using spears will take a lot of Fire charms, because Melee is in the Fire Aspect domain. The vast majority of all DB charms seem to be element-neutral once you get outside the fluff, and the ones that aren't have fairly small differences depending on the user's Aspect.<br /> <br /> No Dragonblood has the ability to actually control the element of their aspect except in fairly superficial ways, or by using very specific charms. Being able to attack people directly using your element requires a Lore charm for some reason. True elemental power is the domain of Sorcerers only. That leaves most DBs with the potential to be sort of generically badass with mostly undeveloped elemental themes.<br /> <br /> I look over everything I just wrote and I don't really see a rhyme or reason to it, beyond possibly a half-assed attempt to pidgeonhole the Dragonbloods into a similar design pattern to the one used for Solars. They certainly are not anything like Benders, despite all those <a href=\"http://rpg.go-ghoti.com/Motivators/Elder%20Dragon%20Blooded.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">demotivational posters</a> out there. So... what exactly are the Elemental Chosen supposed to <i>be</i>, once you get all the cultural baggage about the Realm and breeding and not being Celestials out of the way?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T12:48:45-07:00","id":102114,"title":"","content":"They are the children of the Elemental Dragons. That is what defines the nature of their Exaltation, the nature of their Charms and their place within the setting. Second edition just did a really bad job of getting that across. You fix the problem mostly by giving the Dragon-Blooded charms that do different things depending on the user's Aspect, instead of tying entire Charm trees to a specific element.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T12:56:21-07:00","id":102117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102114#post102114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You fix the problem mostly by giving the Dragon-Blooded charms that do different things depending on the user's Aspect, instead of tying entire Charm trees to a specific element.</div> </div> </div> </div>That... sounds like it would take tremendous wordcount. Approximately five times as much as is currently in the book, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T13:08:20-07:00","id":102125,"title":"","content":"Perhaps Semicasual - but most of my favorite DB charms are the ones that have aspect-specific effects<br /> <br /> Also, another important aspect of DBs is their ability to do team-work and augment mortals they're leading via their special excellency","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T13:44:28-07:00","id":102135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102117#post102117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That... sounds like it would take tremendous wordcount. Approximately five times as much as is currently in the book, actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering what was originally in the MoEP Dragonblooded for 2E, I'd take a hit on charm quantity for charm quality any day for Dragonblooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2394-grifnir","name":"Grifnir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T13:53:42-07:00","id":102140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me#post102106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been reflecting lately on a somewhat unsatisfactory experience of playing a DB, and realized that I really don't get what DBs are really about.<br /> <br /> They're a type of Ability exalted, similar to Solars, but their Abilities are tied to their Aspects through what seems to be mostly thought-association rather than caste-role. Sometimes the association makes sense (Air=flying, flying=Throwing. OK!), and sometimes it doesn't (Arrow shafts are made of Wood. Wood=Archery?), and sometimes it seems to be based more on some kind of idea of Humorism (Fire= choleric, choleric = Presence?).</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me try to address this: (At least how i see this)<br /> <b>Air -</b><br /> Linguistics - Air is about language and communication.<br /> Lore - Knowledge is part of the element of air, and in fact, if you directly translate from hebrew, all the knowledges, like Philosophy and such are called &quot;Air Sciences&quot;.<br /> Occult - A continuation of the Lore idea.<br /> Stealth - Air can move about unseen, and sometimes unfelt, if it moves slowly enough.<br /> Thrown - While Air travels far, it is most damaging in immediate short blasts, like Thrown.<br /> <br /> <b>Earth -</b><br /> Awareness - The Earth is a great way to sense someone approaching, whether you go up a hill, or put your ear to the ground. A bit shaky, but ok.<br /> Craft - People generally like to see their creations stand the test of time, so it's like giving them the permanence of Earth. Also, in ancient times it was rocks, and metals mined from the earth, and clay, who were among the first crafts of our ancestors.<br /> Integrity - Again Earth's permanence. It's like talking to a wall when trying to convince them.<br /> Resistance - And yet again Earth's permanence, where it's harder to cause you damage.<br /> War - Another a bit shaky, but smashing your armies against the city walls is probably a good reason.<br /> <br /> <b>Fire - </b><br /> Athletics - Not sure, but I'd say it's the fact that Fire can move fast in a tinder field, and consumes all in it's path.<br /> Dodge - It's hard to hit something that has no real substance, and that you know can damage you.<br /> Melee - The sparks of the clashing of weapons. Shaky, I agree.<br /> Presence - Fire, of all the elements, has long captivated the mind and imagination of humans.<br /> Socialize - Again, as above. Add in the native americans reference to alcohol as &quot;fire water&quot;, and you get the party boosting powers in Socialize.<br /> <br /> <b>Water -</b><br /> Bureaucracy - It's about the flow of an organization, whether disrupting it, or aiding it.<br /> Investigation - Water gets into every nook and crevice, and if you flood a place, you can find hidden things.<br /> Larceny - Water in world mythology has a tendency to hide things in it's depths.<br /> Martial Arts - Martial Arts are about adapting your Essence to another form, and water is all about adaptation.<br /> Sail - Need i even explain? Water, Ships, they go together.<br /> <br /> <b>Wood - </b><br /> Archery - Bows and arrows have long been made of bows, even until recent times.<br /> Medicine - Plants were always a basic source of medicine<br /> Performance - Many musical instruments are made of wood. A bit shaky. It might also be the fact that nature, portrayed mostly as forests, has always seemed harmonious to us.<br /> Ride - it is with plants, food, that humans first began to domesticate some animals. it is another part of the connection to nature.<br /> Survival - Forests, and heavy plants, were great cover, and may seem harmonious, but they can hide predators in them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Everyone has their own opinions on how the different Abilities should correlate to different Elements, but at the end of the day, the idea was that most of their low-level powers are still sort-of human, and only going deeper into the trees, do they really start manifesting their elemental powers more forcefully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/721-greyskull","name":"Greyskull","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T13:57:10-07:00","id":102146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102114#post102114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are the children of the Elemental Dragons. That is what defines the nature of their Exaltation, the nature of their Charms and their place within the setting. Second edition just did a really bad job of getting that across. You fix the problem mostly by giving the Dragon-Blooded charms that do different things depending on the user's Aspect, instead of tying entire Charm trees to a specific element.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember correctly the developers have said that they plan on doing exactly this. Adding more charms with different effects for each element, and even adding charms that are entirely out of the primary element for an ability's charm tree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T14:06:27-07:00","id":102152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102146#post102146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I remember correctly the developers have said that they plan on doing exactly this. Adding more charms with different effects for each element, and even adding charms that are entirely out of the primary element for an ability's charm tree.</div> </div> </div> </div>The developers said, &quot;WE decide where to spend wordcount now!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T14:40:30-07:00","id":102179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyskull</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Wood - </b><br /> Archery - Bows and arrows have long been made of <b>bows</b>, even until recent times.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure only Abyssals and Fair Folk could use that to any great effect. Shooting bows out of bows? Only true killers and madmen would try that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T14:47:56-07:00","id":102180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me#post102106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I look over everything I just wrote and I don't really see a rhyme or reason to it, beyond possibly a half-assed attempt to pidgeonhole the Dragonbloods into a similar design pattern to the one used for Solars. They certainly are not anything like Benders, despite all those <a href=\"http://rpg.go-ghoti.com/Motivators/Elder%20Dragon%20Blooded.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">demotivational posters</a> out there. So... what exactly are the Elemental Chosen supposed to <i>be</i>, once you get all the cultural baggage about the Realm and breeding and not being Celestials out of the way?</div> </div> </div> </div>To begin with, I will recognise that your criticism has some merit. The way the Abilities get distributed to the Aspects are not always coherent or obvious. I personally think that's mostly a matter of working with what you got. The way the game is designed, you will have twenty-five Abilities to put into five themed categories (even in 3e, where as mentioned they plan on making &quot;off-Aspect&quot; Charms, they still have to come up with a baseline to work from, a way to group the basic Abilities into neat groups of five), and the result will always be someone's subjective idea of the best compromise.<br /> <br /> On a tangent, I personally don't even think that's the biggest problem with the Terrestrial Aspects and their Ability distribution. The fact that your Aspect determines 1) your elemental theme as a whole, 2) your favoured Abilities to the point of putting a surcharge on mote costs when going outside them and 3) your general emotional and psychological direction is at <i>least one</i> too much.<br /> <br /> However, you ask about the Terrestrial design paradigm. In this thread, it's so far only been about how the elemental part is handled. That's fine and all, we can talk about that, but if we want to talk about the Terrestrial design paradigm as a whole, it's imperative to remember that elemental themes are not supposed to be their whole idea. Family and warfare are also equally important, which shows up in their Charmsets in different ways. Sometimes perhaps in ways they shouldn't, but many of my favourite Terrestrial Charms borrow from those instead of the elemental theme. Again, not saying you can't complain about the Aspects, but if you feel you're failing to understand the Terrestrial design paradigm, it might be because you're not looking at all of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T14:53:12-07:00","id":102183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me#post102106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... what exactly are the Elemental Chosen supposed to <i>be</i>, once you get all the cultural baggage about the Realm and breeding and not being Celestials out of the way?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're the great multitude of philosopher-warriors/scholar-bureaucrats who are fit to serve as the army and administration of the ancient Realm. The elemental stuff primarily adds more mystical flavour to them, as well as a suitable hook into different approaches to being a warrior/bureaucrat that is a bit more interesting than just plain saying it. That and how they all work better if we wrap their themes in mythological motifs; like, you could just have Solars as &quot;warrior/leader/etc.&quot; and just have their Charms as out-of-character abstractions, it's just more fun to call Achilles a Dawn Caste and add Appolonian symbolism to his attacks.<br /> <br /> The elements really edge quite close to being entirely arbitrary, even if I personally ascribe to them a relevance of representing a complex, interdependent system.<br /> <br /> Which... does kind of lead into some of their inspiration points, like any Asian tactical manuals that use the mysticism behind Chinese elements as a reference point for various combat principles, so there's that as well.<br /> <br /> Really, in any comparisons to Avatar, the Dragon Blooded are best compared not to the actual <i>feats</i> of Benders, but to their underlying principles and mysticism. Maybe your Earth Aspect will never quite be able to do things that Bumi or Toph do, but they can still live according to ideas of subtlety and carefully chosen moments, and/or by being staid, firm and shiftless; indeed, that's what they're pretty much all doing.<br /> <br /> Aspect Abilities are a thing, but they're mostly an idea of what kinds of skillsets your emotional outlook and the physical and mystical manifestations of your element would give you an affinity for. That's what Aspect Abilities mean more than any kind of social role or anything. Like, there's an intellectual edge to all Air Aspects, so they can basically all be good at what Lore and Occult is, but that doesn't mean that all Air Aspects are scholars (although in the overall schema of some Dragon Blooded organisations, there might be a bit of a bias to make all Air Aspects learn the necessary skills to become scholars). There'll still be Air Aspected swordfighters, and they can even develop some (or possibly many) Charms that use the air element or some resonant principles to be good at it, but the emotional outlook is not so assumed to be generally drawn to it or most strongly expressed by it. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T15:05:51-07:00","id":102194,"title":"","content":"What are the Dragon Blooded? They are the greatest chefs in Creation of course!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T16:35:40-07:00","id":102240,"title":"","content":"Obligatory, because someone's going to say it sooner or later: they're the mook exalted, created by Gaia's equivalent of third-circle souls rather than a proper Incarnae, brought into the world to serve as the minions of the Solars, and as the weakest splat they're also the characters most likely to die first in any given encounter. That's probably the meanest possible way to say it, but as long as we're here we may as well cover why it is or isn't true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T16:55:40-07:00","id":102252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102240#post102240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obligatory, because someone's going to say it sooner or later: they're the mook exalted</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, might as well go through it, like you say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102240#post102240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">created by Gaia's equivalent of third-circle souls rather than a proper Incarnae</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, the Dragons are not the third-circle souls of Gaia. That's been explicitly stated by the developers. We don't know what they are, but we know what they are not. Indeed, that includes Incarnae, but then I ask, does that matter? In 3e, we've been told that Exigents created by Terrestrial gods can be of wildly varying power, up to and including rivalling Solars. I don't think we'll be able to see evidence of too great a correlation between the power level of the source and that of the Exalt in 3e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102240#post102240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">brought into the world to serve as the minions of the Solars</div> </div> </div> </div>Just like the Lunars and the Sidereals, as it were. Just like them, serving a purpose in the design of the Exalted host. It's entirely likely that without the Terrestrials, the Exalted would have lost the Primordial war. This is probably even more true in 3e, where the focus on infrastructure and supportive organisations are being made more important for Solars to utilize their full potential.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102240#post102240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and as the weakest splat they're also the characters most likely to die first in any given encounter.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is harder to refute as it is actually true. Terrestrials are supposed to win by numbers and team tactics, and that might mean losing a soldier to win the battle. But in any given battle? I beg to differ. Terrestrials are supposed to work in teams, so it's hardly &quot;cheating&quot; for them to bring an army. In fact, with non-broken SMA, I'd say a Terrestrial versus a caught-on-his-ass Sidereal is not a foregone conclusion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102240#post102240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's probably the meanest possible way to say it, but as long as we're here we may as well cover why it is or isn't true.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only thing that's really and properly true is that fact that Terrestrials die the easiest. The other things are false or misleading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T17:48:43-07:00","id":102273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102240#post102240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as the weakest splat they're also the characters most likely to die first in any given encounter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reminded of the most recent episode of Dragonball Z Abridged, where the Androids pleasantly dismiss the idea of attacking Krillin because they don't view him as a threat.<br /> <br /> I mean, if the new system will have tactical scenarios in which going too far in an attack leaves you vulnerable, I'd imagine that can hold up for attacking allies, and Terrestrials might even have Charms that hook off it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T17:55:23-07:00","id":102278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102252#post102252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, might as well go through it, like you say.<br /> <br /> First of all, the Dragons are not the third-circle souls of Gaia. That's been explicitly stated by the developers. We don't know what they are, but we know what they are not.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 3rd Edition, the Elemental Dragons will be Gaia's children.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T19:09:27-07:00","id":102306,"title":"","content":"Can't really remember what the devs say about whether their Abilities are still tied to their Aspected Element, but I sure hope that won't happen. My Storm Summoning Taiko Drummer is still sad that Performance is sitting in Wood-Aspected, not to mention its charms doesn't do anything flowery at all (aside from having plant-y names of course).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T19:31:30-07:00","id":102312,"title":"","content":"Anyone else think that the natural weapon Ability might be better in Wood? It could also fit the adaptation theme because of Wood moving the other elements and being the element of living, and thus experience and growth (and death).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T19:45:38-07:00","id":102321,"title":"","content":"Dragon-Blooded Charms take the Ability in question and puts it through the lens of the element, as the OP described. Sometimes, it's fairly obvious, like Thrown. Sometimes, somewhat less so, like Bureaucracy and water (which I feel is saying something like 'water is like coin and bureaucratic power in how it flows and shifts from person to person). Really, its an arbitrary choice based on slotting the Abilities into the five elements. And that's fine -- a lot of design comes down to arbitrary choices. Some people will key into them better than not.<br /> <br /> It's interesting looking back at the 1e ST guide, actually, and seeing how they were initially thinking of any Ability getting any element. Probably cut that idea due to word count, but it sounds like it's coming back in 3e; every Ability will have every element. Honestly, while it does take more word count, it's not that bad. I once started a project to do the same a few years back. A lot of Charms already there make more sense to me as different elements. Each element doesn't need to be equally represented in each Ability either; some Abilities may favor some elements over others, and that's fine.<br /> <br /> As for how the Charms in 2e represent Dragon-Blooded power? Dragon-Blooded are people of pan-elemental power. While they will favor one element over the rest due to their aspect, their aspect is somewhat more primal in nature than a celestial caste; aspect and the Abilities it's linked to will not match perfectly, what a particular Dragon-Blood peruses as their skills. So, you can easily have an Air swordsman who, while being Air-aspected, has learned a lot of Fire charms. And that's fine, since Dragon-Blooded are pan-elemental Exalted who draw their power from all the Dragons, not just one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T19:52:55-07:00","id":102325,"title":"","content":"The Terrestrial Exalted are soldiers. All of them, every aspect. For the Solars, most of the fight-y bits were put into the Dawn Caste. For the Lunars, their warrior guys are the Full Moons. Sidereals are weird, but they DO have have a Battle Auspice.<br /> <br /> Every Aspect of the Terrestrials is, within itself, some self-sustaining form of warrior and/or soldier. Notice, in fact, how each Aspect has one of the Dawn Caste's abilities. Air has Thrown, Wood has Archery, Fire has Melee, Earth has War and Water has Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> The Celestial Exalted were not built to fight a war. That they did and they won is a testament to their awesome might. They were built to rule and sustain Creation after the war was over. Now Terrestrials, Terrestrials were built to fight a war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1252,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","user":"God_of_Awesome","date":".  Missing word 03-31-2014, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T19:58:59-07:00","id":102332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me#post102106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Aspect of each Dragonblood is not especially important except for the Anima power and class abilities, because every DB can use charms from the entire DB charmset, including those that are not of their element. For example, a Water-Aspect who wants to get good at using spears will take a lot of Fire charms, because Melee is in the Fire Aspect domain. The vast majority of all DB charms seem to be element-neutral once you get outside the fluff, and the ones that aren't have fairly small differences depending on the user's Aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it is important. That 1-mote surcharge adds up when your essence pool is low. It's not a crippling weakness, but it does matter, and it's a lot more of an issue than for anyone else. Solars can use charms from the entire Solar charmset without the extra mote cost, the same with Lunars, Sidereals, etc.<br /> <br /> But saying that, I don't think the DB charmset goes into their themes as much as it should (though it's better post-1000 correct actions). As you say, a lot of stuff is element-neutral, and also the co-operation theme that's supposed to be a big part of their charmset isn't actually huge. I virtually never see co-operative charms used in-game.<br /> I think these are issues likely to be sorted out with the next charmset though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T21:34:59-07:00","id":102377,"title":"","content":"On a quick thought while half-asleep, Dragonblooded do seem to suffer from a bit of the other side of the Sidereal's coin. Basically, since the assumed game experience is Solars, both Sidereals and Terrestrials historically seem to have been more designed as what would be good for NPCs than as a fully PC splat. <br /> <br /> The difference being that Sidereals have been more made to be thematically interesting and intriguing antagonists with little rhyme to actually being easy to play in a Sidereal campaign, while Terrestrail seem more the opposite, made to be immediately useful antagonists without too much thought put into thematic consistence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T23:34:22-07:00","id":102440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102183#post102183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">shiftless</div> </div> </div> </div>That word does not mean what you think it means.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102278#post102278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 3rd Edition, the Elemental Dragons will be Gaia's children.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cite?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T23:39:28-07:00","id":102444,"title":"","content":"I never got what the problem was with the five dragons being Gaia's five sub-souls. Surely it makes sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T23:51:11-07:00","id":102458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102444#post102444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never got what the problem was with the five dragons being Gaia's five sub-souls. Surely it makes sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is, it was an attempt at being clever for no reason at all. It probably makes sense, but it's unnecessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T23:52:28-07:00","id":102459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102440#post102440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cite?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To clarify, the Five Elemental Dragons are the Children of Gaia. They are not her souls. <b>(John M\u00f8rke)</b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T00:06:00-07:00","id":102464,"title":"","content":"&quot;What is a Dragon Blooded? A miserable little pile of elements! But enough talk... have at you!&quot; - Lyta<br /> <br /> My group and I were never big fans of this aspect of Dragon Blooded. We all generally liked strong visual themes in our characters and tended to find Dragon Blooded all over the place. When I make a Wood Aspect, I don't really want to be shooting out fire or ice. I want my powers to reflect the fact that I'm Wood Aspect. So when I use a charm like Bellows-Pumping Stride, I don't want to leave flaming, fiery footprints in my wake. I'd much rather be leaving growths of flowers or grass with each step. <br /> <br /> So we ended up reskinning just about all the Dragon Blooded charms so that the visual effects of the charm reflect the Aspect of the user, because we thought that was a bit cooler. <br /> <br /> That worked well enough for us as a quick fix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T00:24:33-07:00","id":102471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102464#post102464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;What is a Dragon Blooded? A miserable little pile of elements! But enough talk... have at you!&quot; - Lyta<br /> <br /> My group and I were never big fans of this aspect of Dragon Blooded. We all generally liked strong visual themes in our characters and tended to find Dragon Blooded all over the place. When I make a Wood Aspect, I don't really want to be shooting out fire or ice. I want my powers to reflect the fact that I'm Wood Aspect. So when I use a charm like Bellows-Pumping Stride, I don't want to leave flaming, fiery footprints in my wake. I'd much rather be leaving growths of flowers or grass with each step.<br /> <br /> So we ended up reskinning just about all the Dragon Blooded charms so that the visual effects of the charm reflect the Aspect of the user, because we thought that was a bit cooler.<br /> <br /> That worked well enough for us as a quick fix.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I prefer DBs as well. I worked with a couple friends in making each Charmset kind of 'closed', having offense and defense and some social capability within all Aspects (like 1e Air signaled towards with Linguistics and Thrown); worked like a charm, and it is how I prefer to see the Dragon-Blooded. They should be pretty much Benders, as well, just more with specific techniques than as freeform (and it is arguable how alot of Avatar works, as well; the air-ball was Aang's technique, the earth-armor seemed to be Toph's signature, and so on.<br /> <br /> Also, most of the abilities seem to fit very well the Aspect. Presence is not only because Fire is choleric; it certainly has presence, illuminating, catching the eye, and even going so far as to sear the vision of those who stare for too long. It would not fit in any other aspect. Same for... most others.<br /> <br /> (Pretty much all of them but Earth have some good claim at Athletics and a couple others, however.)<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the Children of Gaia thing, I think the thinking is that Third Circles makes them seem mundane, lesser, and being Children makes them the same ineffable sort of being as the Incarna, thus defusing precisely the sort of comment HK-87 made earlier. They are actual Exalted, from an actual powerful patron, not an Exalted-like thing made by lesser beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T01:47:15-07:00","id":102499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102278#post102278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In 3rd Edition, the Elemental Dragons will be Gaia's children.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder who their father is ? Hmm, Luna won't be happy to hear that Gaia is into self-impregnate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T02:28:44-07:00","id":102508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--g