com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T03:21:19-07:00","id":102529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102499#post102499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder who their father is ? Hmm, Luna won't be happy to hear that Gaia is into self-impregnate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Midichlorians did it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T03:27:59-07:00","id":102532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Root</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102521#post102521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if we'll see the Great Houses each have a few Charms that reflect their distinct tendencies and methods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems unlikely, or at least unlikely that they'd be ones in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T03:43:51-07:00","id":102536,"title":"","content":"If they introduce bloodline Charms, it would seem very strange if they didn't give a few to the most prominent bloodlines in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T03:58:23-07:00","id":102539,"title":"","content":"I take it you're thinking of Bloodline charms as charms you take for a bloodline you're in, as opposed to 2nd ed's Bloodline charms as high-essence charms that do things for your descendants?<br /> <br /> Because otherwise, I don't see that they'd be unique to that House (which I assume is what Root is wondering about). Obviously saying &quot;Mnemon herself knows these Bloodline charms, Ragara himself knows these Bloodline charms, etc&quot; is a bit different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T08:03:45-07:00","id":102625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102180#post102180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On a tangent, I personally don't even think that's the biggest problem with the Terrestrial Aspects and their Ability distribution. The fact that your Aspect determines 1) your elemental theme as a whole, 2) your favoured Abilities to the point of putting a surcharge on mote costs when going outside them and 3) your general emotional and psychological direction is at <i>least one</i> too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, I actually like the elemental nature/psyche aspect of DBs. It's actually kind of interesting to see precisely <i>how</i> the element expresses itself in a person, and the broadness of scope is sufficient to allow both Peleps Deled and the majority of house Peleps to be Water Aspects, for one example, so it's not really all that restrictive. And determining elemental theme is, well, kind of going to be a given. XD<br /> <br /> But anyway, as to the topic of the thread--Dragon-Blooded don't just manipulate the elements in people, they manipulate the elements in themselves--change the fires in their heart to match the fires in yours, guide their inner earth around an inner flame, and so forth. There is also, as Weimann and others have said, a distinct non-elemental theme that intersects with that in a way I think is beneficial to them--they're nobility. And that's one of my favorite things about them, by the way, if people try to narrow them down to benders I'll be quite annoyed. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/781-chained-divinity","name":"Chained Divinity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar781_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T08:47:30-07:00","id":102655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chained Divinity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102625#post102625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Frankly, I actually like the elemental nature/psyche aspect of DBs. It's actually kind of interesting to see precisely <i>how</i> the element expresses itself in a person, and the broadness of scope is sufficient to allow both Peleps Deled and the majority of house Peleps to be Water Aspects, for one example, so it's not really all that restrictive. And determining elemental theme is, well, kind of going to be a given. XD<br /> <br /> But anyway, as to the topic of the thread--Dragon-Blooded don't just manipulate the elements in people, they manipulate the elements in themselves--change the fires in their heart to match the fires in yours, guide their inner earth around an inner flame, and so forth. There is also, as Weimann and others have said, a distinct non-elemental theme that intersects with that in a way I think is beneficial to them--they're nobility. And that's one of my favorite things about them, by the way, if people try to narrow them down to benders I'll be quite annoyed.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Benders&quot; is actually a wider design space than the DBs currently possess, at least in terms of their elemental abilities. There are a lot of ways to have a character who uses Water to do stuff, or who utilizes Water in addition to something else that they specialize in. As it stands now, Dragonblooded elemental powers practically don't exist - it's easier to make a character with no practical applications of actual elemental force (besides the anima banner) than it is to make a &quot;bender&quot; of any stripe.<br /> <br /> Also, not every Dragonblood comes from Lookshy or the Blessed Isle. If it's not too much to ask, I'd like it to still be possible to make an interesting (and capable!) outcaste DB using only the basis of the Five Dragons' power, in the absence of wealth, followers, or status.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T09:06:59-07:00","id":102673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102655#post102655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Benders&quot; is actually a wider design space than the DBs currently possess, at least in terms of their elemental abilities. There are a lot of ways to have a character who uses Water to do stuff, or who utilizes Water in addition to something else that they specialize in. As it stands now, Dragonblooded elemental powers practically don't exist - it's easier to make a character with no practical applications of actual elemental force (besides the anima banner) than it is to make a &quot;bender&quot; of any stripe.</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of their obviously elemental abilities, yes, but the huge additional versatility of the non-elemental--or, more accurately, not <i>obviously</i> elemental--abilities isn't something to be completely discounted. <br /> <br /> And they really <i>do</i> have a plethora of elemental powers as-is. There's Elemental Bolt, Elemental Concentration and the Immaculate styles, first of all, but there's also an Air Aspect Stealth Charm that creates silence in an area by sucking out any of the wind that was affected by sound, multiple straight-up terrain manipulation things in war, Elemental Defense Technique, the DB near-perfect...oh, also Blinding Spark Distraction and Refining the Inner Blade or whatever it's called. It's entirely easy to make a DB character that expresses their power <i>primarily</i> through the elements, in fact (though a bit harder for Wood Aspects, I'll admit). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, not every Dragonblood comes from Lookshy or the Blessed Isle. If it's not too much to ask, I'd like it to still be possible to make an interesting (and capable!) outcaste DB using only the basis of the Five Dragons' power, in the absence of wealth, followers, or status. </div> </div> </div>It can be possible to do that without ignoring the fact that the Blessed Isle and Lookshy are iconic examples of what DB are.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/781-chained-divinity","name":"Chained Divinity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar781_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T09:18:41-07:00","id":102686,"title":"","content":"I'd point out that the Blessed Isle and Lookshy are not the only places with Nobility. I'd venture to say that Terrestrials tend to create dynasties/noble houses anywhere they linger because they are powerful(just like all other Exalted/Supernatural beings). Moreover, given the mechanics of Dragonblooded Exaltation, they're better at such things, because when a DB dies a DB of the family takes over, rather than just leaving a power vacuum. It's not perfect, especially if the house doesn't have any Dragonblooded at the moment(which wouldn't be uncommon for Outcaste houses), but it's better than the almost certainty of Celestial power transfers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T09:53:05-07:00","id":102726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102655#post102655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Benders&quot; is actually a wider design space than the DBs currently possess, at least in terms of their elemental abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're begging the question here, honestly. Benders is a wider design space in terms of <i>bending</i>. Bending is intentionally not the DB's core gimmick. But Smoke Incense Ladder is an &quot;elemental ability&quot;. DBs have a much wider design space in their powers and their powers are overwhelmingly elemental abilities, it's just that people are looking for elemental wizard telekinesis, and a minority of their elemental abilities express themselves that way. But while &quot;there aren't enough powers that let me shoot flames and shape earth&quot; is a legitimate opinion, the notion that Dragon-Blooded's elemental aptitudes are fake or ill-used on that account is tired.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T11:38:58-07:00","id":102810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102726#post102726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're begging the question here, honestly. Benders is a wider design space in terms of <i>bending</i>. Bending is intentionally not the DB's core gimmick. But Smoke Incense Ladder is an &quot;elemental ability&quot;. DBs have a much wider design space in their powers and their powers are overwhelmingly elemental abilities, it's just that people are looking for elemental wizard telekinesis, and a minority of their elemental abilities express themselves that way. But while &quot;there aren't enough powers that let me shoot flames and shape earth&quot; is a legitimate opinion, the notion that Dragon-Blooded's elemental aptitudes are fake or ill-used on that account is tired.</div> </div> </div> </div>True enough.<br /> <br /> I suppose I'm sore about it mostly because the last two DBs (Air and Wood Aspects) I tried to make were both heavily invested in Sorcery because there was no other way I could enable them to manipulate wind and plants, respectively. Playing with the elements wasn't all they did - the Air Aspect was a bookish academic, a Dynast scholar who had basically been pushed into a Wyld Hunt against his better judgement, while the Wood Aspect was an Outcaste one-woman militia, trying to gain recognition by putting her self-taught fighting skills to work hunting monsters. Both of them had skillsets that made sense for their backgrounds. The problem was that during the character conception phase, both of them had a seed of &quot;Elemental Superhero&quot; that didn't really get to sprout. The Air Aspect couldn't create wind blasts when he was startled (which happened a lot - Valor 1), and the Wood Aspect couldn't wrap enemies in vines unless they spent a lot of BP on extraciricular stuff. It felt like an arbitrary restriction that made the characters mechanically weaker and less focused than they could have been.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T11:57:49-07:00","id":102826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102240#post102240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obligatory, because someone's going to say it sooner or later: they're the mook exalted, created by <u>Gaia's equivalent of third-circle souls rather than a proper Incarnae, brought into the world to serve as the minions of the Solars,</u> and as the weakest splat they're also the characters most likely to die first in any given encounter. That's probably the meanest possible way to say it, but as long as we're here we may as well cover why it is or isn't true.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always kinda thought Gaia made them to keep an eye on the Solars and destroy them after the war, which they did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T12:21:02-07:00","id":102843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102810#post102810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True enough.<br /> <br /> I suppose I'm sore about it mostly because the last two DBs (Air and Wood Aspects) I tried to make were both heavily invested in Sorcery because there was no other way I could enable them to manipulate wind and plants, respectively. Playing with the elements wasn't all they did - the Air Aspect was a bookish academic, a Dynast scholar who had basically been pushed into a Wyld Hunt against his better judgement, while the Wood Aspect was an Outcaste one-woman militia, trying to gain recognition by putting her self-taught fighting skills to work hunting monsters. Both of them had skillsets that made sense for their backgrounds. The problem was that during the character conception phase, both of them had a seed of &quot;Elemental Superhero&quot; that didn't really get to sprout. The Air Aspect couldn't create wind blasts when he was startled (which happened a lot - Valor 1), and the Wood Aspect couldn't wrap enemies in vines unless they spent a lot of BP on extraciricular stuff. It felt like an arbitrary restriction that made the characters mechanically weaker and less focused than they could have been.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like the fact that DBs don't tend toward &quot;elemental superhero&quot; by default, but what we've heard so far makes me think it'll be a bit easier to build toward that niche if you want to. I suspect the &quot;DBs will be unusually good at Evocations within a certain scope&quot; thing we've heard dropped is meant to make it easier for them to have lavish elemental effects without Sorcery, and John mentioned a while ago that he was considering having some more &quot;bendery&quot; MA styles in the DB book. A lot can change between then and when their hardback comes out, but that tells me that it's something the devs have in mind, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T14:34:12-07:00","id":102941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102528#post102528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As soon as they have distinct tendencies and methods...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes... to me that sounds like a worthwhile addition to the game. I remember reading something about the choice of House becoming more significant. Adding mechanical significance certainly could be part of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T15:11:41-07:00","id":102960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102325#post102325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Lunars, their warrior guys are the Full Moons.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Changing Moon begs to differ, as he charges forward in the form of a tiger, at the head of his personally trained, supernaturally-confident cavalry, his Charms making him too beautiful to strike, too terrifying to fight, and so convincingly expressive that his victims fall for his every feint.<br /> <br /> No Moons likewise have the Charms for sniping, fast reactions, and combat sorcery from the skies.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Terrestrial Exalted are all soldiers regardless of Aspect, but the Lunar Exalted are likewise all barbaric warriors regardless of Caste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T16:46:55-07:00","id":102999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102810#post102810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose I'm sore about it mostly because the last two DBs (Air and Wood Aspects) I tried to make were both heavily invested in Sorcery because there was no other way I could enable them to manipulate wind and plants, respectively. Playing with the elements wasn't all they did - the Air Aspect was a bookish academic, a Dynast scholar who had basically been pushed into a Wyld Hunt against his better judgement, while the Wood Aspect was an Outcaste one-woman militia, trying to gain recognition by putting her self-taught fighting skills to work hunting monsters. Both of them had skillsets that made sense for their backgrounds. The problem was that during the character conception phase, both of them had a seed of &quot;Elemental Superhero&quot; that didn't really get to sprout. The Air Aspect couldn't create wind blasts when he was startled (which happened a lot - Valor 1), and the Wood Aspect couldn't wrap enemies in vines unless they spent a lot of BP on extraciricular stuff. It felt like an arbitrary restriction that made the characters mechanically weaker and less focused than they could have been.</div> </div> </div> </div>So do the explanations on what the design paradigm actually is help any?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T17:04:17-07:00","id":103007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102999#post102999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So do the explanations on what the design paradigm actually is help any?</div> </div> </div> </div>Insofar as I have adjusted my expectations, yes. Still think the ability spread and cross-Aspect mote surcharges are annoying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T17:04:29-07:00","id":103008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102528#post102528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As soon as they have distinct tendencies and methods...</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't already?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T17:15:24-07:00","id":103011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=103007#post103007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Insofar as I have adjusted my expectations, yes. Still think the ability spread and cross-Aspect mote surcharges are annoying.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, I don't really want to gimp myself completely by making an air aspect archer who focuses on dodge for his defense. I'd get mote tapped instantly. Either get rid of those surcharges or close off the other aspect abilities completely, right now they're kind of a trap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T17:59:25-07:00","id":103034,"title":"","content":"The ability spread makes more sense when you grok the difference between castes and aspects, but the more surcharge was indeed a terrible idea and I hope 3e jettisons it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T18:09:04-07:00","id":103043,"title":"","content":"Mote surcharges were indeed a bad idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T19:13:21-07:00","id":103064,"title":"","content":"I do wonder whether the idea of Bender DB will still be popular if Avatar has never existed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T19:23:09-07:00","id":103067,"title":"","content":"While I didn't like the mote surcharge, I DID think it was incredibly neat when you got to harmonize those elements to offset it after mastering one of the Five Dragon Styles. And, of course, the Most Beneficent Seed of the Five Dragons was neat for that, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T20:05:34-07:00","id":103092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=103064#post103064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do wonder whether the idea of Bender DB will still be popular if Avatar has never existed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Characters with elemental powers are a cornerstone of JRPGs. It took reading through the DB Charm trees for me to realize that they <i>couldn't</i> actually do things like that outside Elemental Bolt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T20:19:17-07:00","id":103101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=103092#post103092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Characters with elemental powers are a cornerstone of JRPGs. It took reading through the DB Charm trees for me to realize that they <i>couldn't</i> actually do things like that outside Elemental Bolt.</div> </div> </div> </div>And before Avatar, we had the Immaculate Styles which allowing for bending tricks like causing earthquakes and opening earth pits under your opponent.<br /> <br /> Even Aang's &quot;Spirit Bending&quot; trick was preceded by Wood Dragon Style, of &quot;making your soul fall off&quot; fame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T20:22:47-07:00","id":103104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=103043#post103043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mote surcharges were indeed a bad idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I'm not sure different mote costs for in-/out-of-Aspect Charms is a good idea at all, but this was not the way to go about it. Framing matters, and the presentation on it seemed doomed from the word &quot;go.&quot; If they were set on going for it, it would have probably worked out better just to make every Charm 1 mote* higher and say that every in-Aspect Charm gets a mote <i>discount</i>. The numbers functionally work out the same, but this presentation would put more emphasis on, &quot;These are my greatest strengths,&quot; whereas the present set-up has more emphasis on, &quot;Everything else is my huge weakness.&quot;<br /> <br /> * I'm none too familiar with Dragon-Blooded mechanics. However many motes their surcharge is, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T21:43:17-07:00","id":103152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=103064#post103064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do wonder whether the idea of Bender DB will still be popular if Avatar has never existed.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I read MoEP: DBs, I'd never heard of Avatar. And when I read MoEP: DBs, I was baffled by how few Charms they had that actually related to the elements.<br /> <br /> The overall impression I got from the 2E charmset wasn't &quot;elemental supersoldiers.&quot; It was &quot;Solars, but less so.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/832-surlyseraph","name":"SurlySeraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T22:01:27-07:00","id":103166,"title":"","content":"Yeah, me too, I wanted to have more people throwing fireballs and so on, but it's not really that great.<br /> This was a long time before I'd seen Avatar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T23:13:03-07:00","id":103204,"title":"","content":"While a few more literal elements in aesthetic and application wouldn't quite go amiss, particularly as regards distinguishing between different Aspects using the same Ability, I'd still maintain that the Dragon Blooded are less Avatar and more the Book of Five Rings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T01:45:59-07:00","id":103265,"title":"","content":"Unless I misremember, I'd read Jukashi saying &quot;Have I mentioned before how a lot of Exalted powers are actually hard to represent in a comic? [...] Similar problems with the Dragon-Blooded. Their powers are elemental in nature, but a lot of them use metaphorical/metaphysical connections rather than directly flinging fire and whatnot around the place.&quot; before opening the DB book for the first time.<br /> <br /> So I can't say I was ever surprised by their lack of &quot;bending&quot; powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T02:35:46-07:00","id":103270,"title":"","content":"I know that some people will hate me for saying this, but Exigent of an elemental-y God will be more appropriate for you if you want to play a Bender.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T02:41:44-07:00","id":103273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=103270#post103270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that some people will hate me for saying this, but Exigent of an elemental-y God will be more appropriate for you if you want to play a Bender.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh, no one should hate you for that. It's like saying &quot;play a Lunar not a Solar if you want to turn into animals.&quot; I know people naturally assume DB's will have element-mancy powers, but I don't think it's ever really stated anywhere that they do. It's not like you're lured in with promises of fireballs and ice beams, then &quot;oops we lied there are none.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/46-oramus","name":"Oramus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar46_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T07:38:02-07:00","id":103379,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's way, way easier to make that kind of elemental powerset on an Exigent. Wasn't there a mention of a volcano exigent that basically worked that way, actually?<br /> <br /> <br /> The basic problem, I think, is that Dragon-Blooded are Ability Exalted, and while I've seen a lot of people dispute the value of that, I like it and it's clearly there for a reason. A lot of the stuff people seem to be asking for fits very poorly into an Ability charm framework, which means that if you go that direction, your powers do not feel like an elementally-powered expression of your Abilities (and more broadly of your specific character), which is the point of taking that approach. You lose a tremendous amount by removing that, so I really do think it's better to just make an exigent if you want something like a native Firebending charm tree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T07:43:57-07:00","id":103384,"title":"","content":"The ability to deal with actual elemental forces is pretty tertiary to what Dragon Blooded do. Instead of describing them as &quot;Elemental Warriors&quot; would probably be better to describe Dragon Blooded as superhumans whose power is &quot;reminiscent&quot; of, or &quot;flavored&quot; by the elements. That way people don't go into it expecting to play Human Torch or Zeus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T08:01:15-07:00","id":103393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=103270#post103270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that some people will hate me for saying this, but Exigent of an elemental-y God will be more appropriate for you if you want to play a Bender.</div> </div> </div> </div>I question the utility of telling people to play an Exalt type that doesn't exist yet and probably won't for another year+.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=103379#post103379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I really do think it's better to just make an exigent if you want something like a native Firebending charm tree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I'll just make an exigent. It's so simple and easy to do, I wonder why I haven't thought of this before?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T08:20:28-07:00","id":103401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=103204#post103204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While a few more literal elements in aesthetic and application wouldn't quite go amiss, particularly as regards distinguishing between different Aspects using the same Ability, I'd still maintain that the Dragon Blooded are less Avatar and more the Book of Five Rings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only a fool would call the <i>Go Rin No Sho</i> &quot;elemental.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T08:37:29-07:00","id":103408,"title":"","content":"The time spent homebrewing an element-bending Exigent might as well be spent homebrewing element-bending DB Charms, with the added bonus of not having to figure out absolutely everything else about how the character will work.<br /> <br /> I mean, we can spend days arguing how much element bending the DB Charmset can or should contain, but it's not like weaponizing elemental manifestations is forbidden design space for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T09:25:31-07:00","id":103439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=103401#post103401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only a fool would call the <i>Go Rin No Sho</i> &quot;elemental.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>'kaaaaaaayyyyy...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=103408#post103408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The time spent homebrewing an element-bending Exigent might as well be spent homebrewing element-bending DB Charms, with the added bonus of not having to figure out absolutely everything else about how the character will work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how pertinent this is, but Imma cite it anyway:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to think of the Dragon-Blooded as specialists, not masters. A Solar, Sidereal, and even sometimes a Lunar might have to worry about drowning. So a hypothetical Exalt who controls water is going to have a problem with a Water Aspect who can move through water like a missile, who can shoot his bow underwater, who doesn't drown and can rise like a mountain from the earth, delivering a punch that puts his foe completely out of the water, where he lands at the feet of his Brotherhood. It's not about being the best at an element.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the grand scheme of what the Terrestrial Exalted for, there's a lot to be said for the approach that using an element as a weapon is a lot less useful than being able to fight unhindered in environmental conditions defined by that element.<br /> <br /> I can imagine that, when the great armies of Medo fall against the supernatural might of the legions of the Realm, that might takes less the form of &quot;they were able to shoot icicles and stuff&quot; and more &quot;they were like Hannibal crossing the Alps, Washington crossing the Delaware, and various European attempts to invade Russia, without the casualties&quot;.<br /> <br /> I do feel a certain appeal in the idea that Terrestrial Exalted manifesting the lower power than Celestials through the lens of elements as more grounded and substantial by being more practically minded than numinous.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T09:37:53-07:00","id":103454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=103393#post103393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I question the utility of telling people to play an Exalt type that doesn't exist yet and probably won't for another year+.<br /> <br /> Okay, I'll just make an exigent. It's so simple and easy to do, I wonder why I haven't thought of this before?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Are you complaining that that &quot;this is more of an Exigent niche&quot; is a bad answer just because the Exigent book will take longer to come out? Solars don't get Sidereal Astrology just because the people who want to play Sidereal Astrologers are <i>antsy</i>. I mean, if the context of the discussion is &quot;I need to play this by the time the Dragon-Blooded book is out or the bomb will go off&quot;...well, no, you should still probably play an Exigent, because they're not going to radically change what Dragon-Blooded are just to serve that need, and homebrewing an Exigent before the Exigent book drops is probably easier than homebrewing the Dragon-Blooded to have a strongly bendery focus.<br /> <br /> For people who are totally hopeless with homebrew, it is worth remembering that even though Exigents are meant to be usable as artisanal bespoke Exalted, there will surely be as many homebrew Exigents published to the web as there have ever been Martial Arts styles or Devil-Tigers or what have you. I have a strong suspicion that this will happen within six to eight months of the release of the corebook, on the basis of nothing more than the core systems and a page or two of text on Exigents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T09:45:57-07:00","id":103460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=103408#post103408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The time spent homebrewing an element-bending Exigent might as well be spent homebrewing element-bending DB Charms, with the added bonus of not having to figure out absolutely everything else about how the character will work.<br /> <br /> I mean, we can spend days arguing how much element bending the DB Charmset can or should contain, but it's not like weaponizing elemental manifestations is forbidden design space for them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This addresses the same basic issue as I tackled in my response to hippokrene, but to expand: I think you're really underestimating how hard this is. Good charm design requires taking the <i>entire </i>context of the charmset into account, so elaborate homebrew charm projects on someone with 300-400 charms are intrinsically more difficult than designing a self-contained, 50-charm set from scratch that never has to interact with other things and doesn't need to fit every possible character concept under the awning of a single splat. It's easy to bolt bending charms onto Dragon-Blooded if you don't care about the end quality of their charmset, and since &quot;quality of charmset&quot; is a difficult thing to assess or get feedback on, people will in fact do this naively. But actually getting good results is much, much easier when designing something small and self-contained, when you don't need to spread out across a vast area or worry about interactions with hundreds of established effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T11:12:57-07:00","id":103505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=103439#post103439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'kaaaaaaayyyyy...</div> </div> </div> </div>The word elemental has connotations that are quite unlike the subtle symbolism of the Book of Five Rings, especially when its used in the context of fantasy. Yet, the books insist on presenting the Terrestrial Exalted as <i>elemental</i> when they're actually martial-with-elemental-symbolism.<br /> <br /> It's cool, but nonintuitive, and so we get this thread in various permutations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T11:20:50-07:00","id":103513,"title":"","content":"Another reason I'm personally attached to the idea that the Terrestrial Exalted are elemental in a more figurative sense is because, otherwise, their role as the Army of the Gods just feels really weird.<br /> <br /> Were it not for the fact that the basic standard for distinctions between the Exalted is already set up across the board as certain mythically resonant aesthetics, I'd actually almost think that they <i>should</i> be more akin to less powerful Solars, because they're already basically the Jade Army that tried to subdue Sun Wukong (and that's what I assume that the Ten Thousand Dragons from Kindred of the East basically were). But there are several reasons why that can't and shouldn't be done, so here we are. It's still not really helpful to take the elemental aesthetics in terms of trying to dodge around the idea that the Dragon Blooded actually are the least powerful of the Exalted.<br /> <br /> As for Avatar, it's a great fantasy martial arts story to be sure, but within its own story the actual substance of the elements is rarely the point, and the degrees of narrative importance ultimately have to map to Exalted with a recognition that Exalted has a much more diverse presence of magic in it; what is Bending in Avatar is distributed through the wide world of supernatural martial arts in Exalted, except for the workhorse stuff that is more thaumaturgy, and some Avatar State stuff that might be more Sorcery. That elemental stuff holds prominence in Avatar shouldn't really impose itself upon an entirely different fiction.<br /> <br /> The idea that the elemental cultural and spiritual themes still map very closely to the Dragon Blooded notwithstanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T12:17:09-07:00","id":103556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=103439#post103439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can imagine that, when the great armies of Medo fall against the supernatural might of the legions of the Realm, that might takes less the form of &quot;they were able to shoot icicles and stuff&quot; and more &quot;they were like Hannibal crossing the Alps, Washington crossing the Delaware, and various European attempts to invade Russia, without the casualties&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not disagreeing, but at the same time, DBs have had a &quot;shoot icicles&quot; Charm for two editions straight, and at least in 2e, it was actually a mandatory starting Charm for Lookshyans, explained as part of their combat doctrine. So at least sometimes, it actually would be &quot;they shot icicles at us&quot;, and that's fine as well.<br /> <br /> Going back to John's example (which I also agree with, to an extent), my point here is, that Water Aspect may shoot his powerbow at the waterbending Exigent, but he might as well hurl balls of water using Elemental Bolt and finish him off with watery Dragon Vortex Attack, at which point I'd say we've got a regular waterbending duel right here, with the DB using nothing but core Charms. And he still retains the advantages John speaks of, because they are independent of his chosen mode of attack. Now, can the Water-Aspect DB win such a waterbending duel against an Exigent? Should he win? Are his chances of winning affected by him choosing elemental attacks over more mundane means which his magic makes compatible with the underwater battlegrounds? Those are all fine points of splat balance that I'd rather not dwell too long upon while we're between editions, and it can certainly go either way depending on many different factors. <br /> <br /> Ultimately, the most important difference between a Water Aspect and a water-themed Exigent is that of style - a DB is limited to Ability-oriented effects where either the effect is colored by symbolic associations of the element, or a manifestation of a raw element serves as a medium through which the effect is achieved. Meanwhile, the Exigent can approach his elemental theme from any angle, and in fact, you can make many Exigents that share the same elemental theme, but remain different between each other and from the DBs of the same element. Doesn't change my point - that being, DBs can play in the same field, even if they play slightly differently.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=103460#post103460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This addresses the same basic issue as I tackled in my response to hippokrene, but to expand: I think you're really underestimating how hard this is. Good charm design requires taking the <i>entire </i>context of the charmset into account, so elaborate homebrew charm projects on someone with 300-400 charms are intrinsically more difficult than designing a self-contained, 50-charm set from scratch that never has to interact with other things and doesn't need to fit every possible character concept under the awning of a single splat. It's easy to bolt bending charms onto Dragon-Blooded if you don't care about the end quality of their charmset, and since &quot;quality of charmset&quot; is a difficult thing to assess or get feedback on, people will in fact do this naively. But actually getting good results is much, much easier when designing something small and self-contained, when you don't need to spread out across a vast area or worry about interactions with hundreds of established effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would have been a concern if I was a writer trying to sell OPP my work on DB &quot;bending&quot; Charms. When I'm a GM and a player tells me: you know, it would be awesome if I could use water to freeze enemies in place like Katara in that one episode, I really, really don't need to even approach that level of scrutiny when I sit down with him and write two or three Charms for him to make that happen. Seriously, it's not even half as hard as you make it out to be. Even with 2e, which is less stable than Gem during the annual firedancing festival.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T12:59:23-07:00","id":103599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=103556#post103556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not disagreeing, but at the same time, DBs have had a &quot;shoot icicles&quot; Charm for two editions straight, and at least in 2e, it was actually a mandatory starting Charm for Lookshyans, explained as part of their combat doctrine. So at least sometimes, it actually would be &quot;they shot icicles at us&quot;, and that's fine as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh certainly. I myself am given to imagine what the battle of Marathon or Cathae would look like if you could lob fireballs into the enveloped mass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T13:15:32-07:00","id":103614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=103599#post103599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh certainly. I myself am given to imagine what the battle of Marathon or Cathae would look like if you could lob fireballs into the enveloped mass.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny how DBs can benefit from a tight combat formation while making the same choice spell suicide for the enemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T17:26:50-07:00","id":103728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=103104#post103104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it would have probably worked out better just to make every Charm 1 mote* higher and say that every in-Aspect Charm gets a mote <i>discount</i>. The numbers functionally work out the same</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, they don't.<br /> <br /> Since First Edition, the mote surcharge only adds one mote to the cost of a single out-of-Aspect Charm per turn. So an Air Aspect using Firecracker Hopping Evasion can use the intended cost of the Charm four times out of five, and the first time only pays one extra mote.<br /> <br /> But if that cost is jacked up by one mote all of the time, and that Air Aspect doesn't enjoy the discount, then she has to pay four extra motes instead of one.<br /> <br /> So, as bad an idea as mote surcharge might be, a higher mote cost in general with a mere discount would be much, much worse.<br /> <br /> <br /> Which is not to say that the discount part of the idea is inherently bad. Perhaps if one kept the costs unchanged and instead allowed a one-mote-per-first-activation-per-Charm discount? That way, a Fire Aspect pays for Firecracker Hopping Evasion more cheaply just the one time per action, but otherwise he and everyone else pays exactly what they are intended to pay.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T17:47:23-07:00","id":103732,"title":"","content":"Mote surcharges are not fun. Mote discounts could have potential, but I dislike players not being able to just look at the cost of a Charm and know what it is\u2014too much book-keeping!<br /> <br /> I've been playing with some ways of incentivizing and rewarding focusing in on Charms of a specific aspect. I hope you'll get to see them!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":18}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T18:03:33-07:00","id":103738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=103728#post103728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*constructive and respectful criticism of my earlier thought*</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahhah! Thank you for clearing up my misunderstanding. This reminds me why half-remembered mechanics mixed with half-remembered forum conversations are not the firmest foundations. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Still, glad the sentiment has some appeal. Thanks for working with the idea.<br /> <br /> @Vance: Also a fair point. Followed by an encouraging, intriguing tidbit to boot. ^_^ Best of luck with your experimenting! If you have any opaque clues you want to share about your ideas, you know this place is the right piranha pool for your discarded cow carcasses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T01:16:38-07:00","id":103902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=103732#post103732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mote surcharges are not fun. Mote discounts could have potential, but I dislike players not being able to just look at the cost of a Charm and know what it is\u2014too much book-keeping!<br /> <br /> I've been playing with some ways of incentivizing and rewarding focusing in on Charms of a specific aspect. I hope you'll get to see them!</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as someone who likes playing In Aspect, even when doing out of aspect things, I like this idea and hope to hear more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T02:46:41-07:00","id":103931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oramus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=103273#post103273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh, no one should hate you for that. It's like saying &quot;play a Lunar not a Solar if you want to turn into animals.&quot; I know people naturally assume DB's will have element-mancy powers, but I don't think it's ever really stated anywhere that they do. It's not like you're lured in with promises of fireballs and ice beams, then &quot;oops we lied there are none.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted First Edition, page 306</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon-Blooded Charms that don\u2019t directly benefit Abilities tend to be elemental in character. These Charms extend not just to hurling elemental bolts, but grant the character an ability to manipulate his element in a more complex fashion. Charms of this sort will be detailed in the Exalted Storytellers Companion.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted Storytellers Companion, page 16</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Charms of the Dragon-Blooded tend to be less powerful overall than the Charms of the Solar, Lunar and Sidereal Exalted. However, a Celestial Exalted cannot equal the facility ofthe Dragon-Blooded at manipulating the actual, physical substance of an element.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those in the most obvious sections, the ones explicitly describing the Dragon-Blooded. So yes, you are lured with such promises, and yes, it is stated that they do have a facility with manipulating actual, physical elements Celestials cannot equal, and that they do indeed hurl elemental bolts.<br /> <br /> I'm sure SEVERAL more examples could be found if one had to really turn this into a job.<br /> <br /> Plus, things like Harmonious Wind-Luring Song and Stone-Carving Fingers Form (which in one minute creates great holes in stone or makes anything out of stone you wish with but a couple strikes upon it, much in the way alot of earthbending worked) have always been there, have always been a thing, and elemental bolt was in since forever.<br /> <br /> DBs always had element-mancy powers and it was the stated core of their charmset. It's a thing. It has always been a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","user":"Colapso","date":". 04-02-2014, 05:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T03:08:35-07:00","id":103939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=103931#post103931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those in the most obvious sections, the ones explicitly describing the Dragon-Blooded. So yes, you are lured with such promises, and yes, it is stated that they do have a facility with manipulating actual, physical elements Celestials cannot equal, and that they do indeed hurl elemental bolts.<br /> <br /> I'm sure SEVERAL more examples could be found if one had to really turn this into a job.<br /> <br /> Plus, things like Harmonious Wind-Luring Song and Stone-Carving Fingers Form (which in one minute creates great holes in stone or makes anything out of stone you wish with but a couple strikes upon it, much in the way alot of earthbending worked) have always been there, have always been a thing, and elemental bolt was in since forever.<br /> <br /> DBs always had element-mancy powers and it was the stated core of their charmset. It's a thing. It has always been a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't speak about First Edition, since I've never played or read it, but it's certainly not an impression I got from second. If you can find some 2e quotes that firmly support DBs being able to physically manipulate their element at will, I'd agree.<br /> <br /> Also, as I was replying to Jen, I suppose I more meant: &quot;if in 3e the DB book says you can sling around water bolts and rock shards, then doesn't support that, that sucks and is bad.&quot;<br /> <br /> Why does this forum have such an awful editor? Mine's jumping focus around the text apparently at random :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/46-oramus","name":"Oramus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar46_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T03:13:43-07:00","id":103941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oramus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=103939#post103939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't speak about First Edition, since I've never played or read it, but it's certainly not an impression I got from second. If you can find some 2e quotes that firmly support DBs being able to physically manipulate their element at will, I'd agree.<br /> <br /> Also, as I was replying to Jen, I suppose I more meant: &quot;if in 3e the DB book says you can sling around water bolts and rock shards, then doesn't support that, that sucks and is bad.&quot;<br /> <br /> Why does this forum have such an awful editor? Mine's jumping focus around the text apparently at random :/</div> </div> </div> </div>Find... second edition... quotes...<br /> <br /> *Laughs incoherently*<br /> <br /> I'm not looking back at those books/re-borrowing them if you paid me to. 2e's hacked and butchered versions of those concepts shouldn't form the basis for what they are.<br /> <br /> And yeah, the editor is really annoying :/ I just copy it all to notepad, write posts there, then paste them in here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T03:17:43-07:00","id":103943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=103941#post103941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 2e's hacked and butchered versions of those concepts shouldn't form the basis for anyone's thoughts on the Exalts.</div> </div> </div> </div> I guess you're right in that the first thing that came to mind when I was told about DBs was elemental manipulation, but I honestly can't recall anything else really supporting that. Especially not enough to make me feel disappointed when reading their Charms and finding out they didn't have that much. But again, I started in 2e.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yeah, the editor is really annoying :/ I just copy it all to notepad, write posts there, then paste them in here. </div> </div> </div> I'm gonna have to start doing that. It's driving me craycray.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/46-oramus","name":"Oramus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar46_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T10:37:08-07:00","id":104142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=103941#post103941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Find... second edition... quotes...<br /> <br /> *Laughs incoherently*<br /> <br /> I'm not looking back at those books/re-borrowing them if you paid me to. 2e's hacked and butchered versions of those concepts shouldn't form the basis for what they are.<br /> <br /> And yeah, the editor is really annoying :/ I just copy it all to notepad, write posts there, then paste them in here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shut <i>up</i>. I am <i>sick to death</i> of <i>everyone</i> on the forum going on and <i>fucking</i> on about what a horrible thing the game that I <i>started</i> on, that <i>made me interested</i> is. I <i>have</i> read the 1st Edition books that were handed out as Kickstarter rewards, and frankly, if your glasses were any more rose-colored, they'd have <i>thorns</i> on.<br /> <br /> <i>Enough</i> with the edition war already!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":17}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T10:58:27-07:00","id":104165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shut <i>up</i>. I am <i>sick to death</i> of <i>everyone</i> on the forum going on and <i>fucking</i> on about what a horrible thing the game that I <i>started</i> on, that <i>made me interested</i> is. I <i>have</i> read the 1st Edition books that were handed out as Kickstarter rewards, and frankly, if your glasses were any more rose-colored, they'd have <i>thorns</i> on.<br /> <br /> <i>Enough</i> with the edition war already!</div> </div> </div> </div>I get where you're coming from. Although I started with 1st edition, the second edition rekindled my table's Exalted spirit and has kept it burning for every year since it first released. It provided a fresh and new combat system that my group, honestly, never had many problems with. We never had that much problem with perfect defenses, we thought every playable race was fun to write up, and we didn't really get bogged down with combat, at least not for a few years. We eventually started noticing, little by little, that Lunar Charms were pretty limited, but even that was offset by Hearts Blood and martial arts.<br /> <br /> And the concepts being hacked or butchered I don't really see... I felt like a lot of the things we did were fun. Maybe I just had a really good group and glossed over anything bad with good Storyteller handling, but seriously, 2nd edition was never as bad as most of the forum rants on about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T12:00:28-07:00","id":104232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=104142#post104142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shut <i>up</i>. I am <i>sick to death</i> of <i>everyone</i> on the forum going on and <i>fucking</i> on about what a horrible thing the game that I <i>started</i> on, that <i>made me interested</i> is. I <i>have</i> read the 1st Edition books that were handed out as Kickstarter rewards, and frankly, if your glasses were any more rose-colored, they'd have <i>thorns</i> on.<br /> <br /> <i>Enough</i> with the edition war already!</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to talk about the parts of 2E I deeply enjoyed, or talk about why I didn't enjoy <i>this</i> part as much as <i>that</i> part. I generally save my ire for Infernals at this point, which hasn't really changed since their book came out, and I said it would lead to bad places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T12:17:26-07:00","id":104240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=104232#post104232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I tend to talk about the parts of 2E I deeply enjoyed, or talk about why I didn't enjoy <i>this</i> part as much as <i>that</i> part. I generally save my ire for Infernals at this point, which hasn't really changed since their book came out, and I said it would lead to bad places.</div> </div> </div> </div>I save mine for Sidereals. Which still suck in 2.5 at all lot of things because they don't have key skills other exalts have and their astrology still sucks. The difference being Astrology has always sucked. The fluff for sidereals is a lot better in first edition though and second editions was awful. I can't wait for 3e sidereals though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T13:24:28-07:00","id":104299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=104142#post104142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shut <i>up</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. I won't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T13:32:58-07:00","id":104306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=104142#post104142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shut <i>up</i>. I am <i>sick to death</i> of <i>everyone</i> on the forum going on and <i>fucking</i> on about what a horrible thing the game that I <i>started</i> on, that <i>made me interested</i> is. I <i>have</i> read the 1st Edition books that were handed out as Kickstarter rewards, and frankly, if your glasses were any more rose-colored, they'd have <i>thorns</i> on.<br /> <br /> <i>Enough</i> with the edition war already!</div> </div> </div> </div>Rose-colored glasses, eh? I started with Second Edition too, and then I went back to read the 1e books mostly out of curiosity. Now, I haven't <i>played</i> 1E, but from what I've heard and read, there's a reason why there was a second edition. The mechanics of 2E, where they weren't ruined by sloppy conversion jobs, are a significant step forward from 1E. The setting information, though? 2E hasn't got a leg to stand on. It's cartoonish in comparison, and full of memes that have done great harm to the game. (DotFA anyone?) There's a reason why there's going to be a third edition, too.<br /> <br /> So no. <i>You</i> shut up with your attempts to silence completely valid criticism. Or better yet, <i>put</i> up, so we can have a discussion with both sides represented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","name":"Schleiermacher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T14:02:41-07:00","id":104326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=104165#post104165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the concepts being hacked or butchered I don't really see...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there is the fact that, in light of how 1e presented the Dragon-Blooded as elemental, an argument was put forth in good faith here that 2e doesn't play up the Elemental mastery aspect of Dragon-Blooded at all. Wouldn't you say that is a problematic presentation of the concept?<br /> <br /> I could probably list a ton, but... really, it would spark an edition-war, and really derail this thread.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't mind making a quick list to you if you want, though, just PM me or something.<br /> <br /> And really, 2e has its good spots. Just the overall presentation of the core concepts was horrible, and shouldn't serve as a guideline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","user":"Colapso","date":". 04-02-2014, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T14:08:34-07:00","id":104327,"title":"","content":"To me DBs are much more the soldier exalted than the elemental exalted. Elemental themes are there but at least as iconic as a fireball, I think, is a bunch of DB hoplites standing shoulder to shoulder in a shield wall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T14:22:51-07:00","id":104335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=104327#post104327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me DBs are much more the soldier exalted than the elemental exalted. Elemental themes are there but at least as iconic as a fireball, I think, is a bunch of DB hoplites standing shoulder to shoulder in a shield wall.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAll Exalted have multiple concepts, though. Solars are just as much Conan as a gleaming golden Fate's Gilgamesh. They are leadership, yes, but also excellence, also humanity, also golden solar flames. Sidereals are astrologers and viziers and mystics and also martial artists and generals and couriers and assassins. <br /> <br /> None of the Exalted are singular in their themes.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T14:23:26-07:00","id":104336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=103732#post103732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mote surcharges are not fun. Mote discounts could have potential, but I dislike players not being able to just look at the cost of a Charm and know what it is\u2014too much book-keeping!<br /> <br /> I've been playing with some ways of incentivizing and rewarding focusing in on Charms of a specific aspect. I hope you'll get to see them!</div> </div> </div> </div>* Mote surcharges are removed! Hurray!<br /> * A rebalancing of the Dragon-Blooded charm set has increased the cost of all charms by one mote.<br /> * In-Aspect charms receive a one mote discount to their use.<br /> <br /> I'm looking forward to seeing the ways you come up with to reward focusing on charms of a specific aspect because you seem to realize that mote discounts are absolutely not the right way to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/407-ithle","name":"Ithle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T16:01:12-07:00","id":104401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, there is the fact that, in light of how 1e presented the Dragon-Blooded as elemental, an argument was put forth in good faith here that 2e doesn't play up the Elemental mastery aspect of Dragon-Blooded at all. Wouldn't you say that is a problematic presentation of the concept?<br /> <br /> I could probably list a ton, but... really, it would spark an edition-war, and really derail this thread.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't mind making a quick list to you if you want, though, just PM me or something.<br /> <br /> And really, 2e has its good spots. Just the overall presentation of the core concepts was horrible, and shouldn't serve as a guideline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. :.P<br /> <br /> Of course, I could be blinded by it all, and meshing the editions together. When we leapt from 1st edition to 2nd edition, we didn't completely just forget everything from the previous edition and start completely fresh. A lot of the ideas were engrained in us and it definitely flavored how we perceived 2nd edition Exalts. Then, we jumped completely on 2.5 and haven't really compared it with how 2nd edition used to be... so perhaps I'm just focusing on all the good points that have gradually increased in quality and kind of blocking out the bad.<br /> <br /> And once Thousand Correct Actions gave me Glorious Birthright Font, I find it hard to see flaws anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T16:15:24-07:00","id":104418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schleiermacher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=104306#post104306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So no. <i>You</i> shut up with your attempts to silence completely valid criticism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nocte and Epimetheus have completely valid criticisms; they identified particular points they found problematic, in neutral language, without attempting to claim that those problems were all that 2E had. Colapso used aggressive language to dismiss and insult the <i>entire edition</i>, and by extension everyone who actually enjoyed it.<br /> <br /> You'll note which I lost my temper at.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schleiermacher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=104306#post104306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or better yet, <i>put</i> up, so we can have a discussion with both sides represented.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, sure. Let's go with the low-hanging fruit and talk about Lunars for a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T16:33:04-07:00","id":104425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=104418#post104418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nocte and Epimetheus have completely valid criticisms; they identified particular points they found problematic, in neutral language, without attempting to claim that those problems were all that 2E had. Colapso used aggressive language to dismiss and insult the <i>entire edition</i>, and by extension everyone who actually enjoyed it.<br /> <br /> You'll note which I lost my temper at.</div> </div> </div> </div>So noted, and it's quite understandable, but you yourself were also tarring with an excessively broad brush, and two wrongs don't make a right. And Colapso has since explained their viewpoint in a more precise and nuanced fashion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=104418#post104418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> OK, sure. Let's go with the low-hanging fruit and talk about Lunars for a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's not, this is a Dragon-Blooded thread. I rather had in mind if you'd care to defend the 2E presentation of Dragon-Blooded, or argue that the 1E presentation wasn't as different as it's been alleged to be. If you have a dog in the fight at all, that is.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","name":"Schleiermacher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T16:58:05-07:00","id":104439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=104418#post104418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Colapso used aggressive language to dismiss and insult the <i>entire edition</i>, and by extension everyone who actually enjoyed it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, it was never my intent to insult the people who enjoyed it. My apologies, Valles. <br /> <br /> However, Oramus did not see value in what I pasted, and asked for 2e quotes. You'll note that's when I used dismissive language.<br /> <br /> And I honestly don't see what's so controversial about what I said, that 2e shouldn't be where we base people's view of the archetypes. There are no 2e books given out in the Kickstarter for a reason, and 3e is going back to the roots of Exalted for a reason. When the argument is put forth that Dragon-Blooded should lose one of their main abilities due to 2e's presentation of them, I find it hard to give it much credit.<br /> <br /> If you wish to make another thread to discuss an edition war, or PM me, though, feel free. Then I'd answer you about the low-hanging fruit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T16:59:21-07:00","id":104440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=104335#post104335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bAll Exalted have multiple concepts, though. Solars are just as much Conan as a gleaming golden Fate's Gilgamesh. They are leadership, yes, but also excellence, also humanity, also golden solar flames. Sidereals are astrologers and viziers and mystics and also martial artists and generals and couriers and assassins.<br /> <br /> None of the Exalted are singular in their themes.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True, I just think their themes are more heavily weighted towards the soldier aspect. The largest tree for them, and indeed one of the largest trees in the entire game, is the DB war tree. They have martial charms in almost every ability, even to the detriment of that ability's function. I think this may become more distinct as in the next edition you can have an exigent of a fire god who IS totally about fire in every way, so DBs are going to be more defined by how they aren't that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T17:09:55-07:00","id":104442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=104440#post104440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> True, I just think their themes are more heavily weighted towards the soldier aspect. The largest tree for them, and indeed one of the largest trees in the entire game, is the DB war tree. They have martial charms in almost every ability, even to the detriment of that ability's function. I think this may become more distinct as in the next edition you can have an exigent of a fire god who IS totally about fire in every way, so DBs are going to be more defined by how they aren't that.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you can also make an Exigent of a God of War, which will be more distinct at that than the Dragon-Blooded. Wouldn't they also have to be defined by how they aren't just a version of, say, Sunipa's Exalted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T17:51:43-07:00","id":104485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=104440#post104440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, I just think their themes are more heavily weighted towards the soldier aspect. The largest tree for them, and indeed one of the largest trees in the entire game, is the DB war tree. They have martial charms in almost every ability, even to the detriment of that ability's function. I think this may become more distinct as in the next edition you can have an exigent of a fire god who IS totally about fire in every way, so DBs are going to be more defined by how they aren't that.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet, their by far most iconic war Charm is a torrent of pure elemental destruction. Not an expression of strategic genius, nor indomitable combat discipline. Pure, unadulterated elemental destruction harnessed for battlefield use.<br /> <br /> Frankly, I think the militant focus of their Charms is more of a cultural thing than a statement on their fundamental nature. Ever since the Ten Thousand Dragons marched against the armies of the Primordials, being soldiers and warriors defined them above everything else, and that cultural definition stuck with them through all the vicissitudes of the ages after. That's why even those DBs whose main forte lies outside the battlefield seek ways to weaponize their talents - something that comes rather easy to them, given the elemental associations of their Charms. But I'm sure there are many Wood Aspects who can give incredible, sensual, pheromone-enhanced performances as readily as they can rip someone apart with ballistic guitar riffs.<br /> <br /> In other words, the way I see it, they are elemental Exalted with solid cultural reasons to put their magical talents to militant use, not soldier Exalted who happen to hurl fireballs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T17:52:19-07:00","id":104486,"title":"","content":"The 1st Edition Aspect Books still hold up as a very good window into the Terrestrial paradigm. Especially Wood, which contains a lot of first-person autobiographical stuff written from the perspective of Tepet Ejava. The entries about her early life really seemed to sum up the ethos of the Dragon-Blooded to me. I guess it's not surprising, considering who she's supposed to be.<br /> <br /> And yeah, it's the soldier aspect. They're not generals, they're soldiers. Even as an aristocracy, they're a military aristocracy. Even the young of the most decadent house, when shown a rack of weapons, can demonstate proficiency with every one. They were bred to be superhuman soldiers. War is in their hearts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T18:27:15-07:00","id":104501,"title":"","content":"The main difference between the &quot;elemental-ness&quot; of 2e's charms and 1e's is that 2e had far more charms that evoked your Aspect rather than that of the charm's Ability, or that had a &quot;module&quot; for each element with you learning your own first. With a couple of exceptions, 1e Dragon-Blooded charms reflected the element of the Ability they were associated with. I think this was a good change, though probably worse than 3e's decision to just have charms of different elements in the same tree. But the 2e charmset only changed DB thematics in subtle and inadvertent ways, by messing up mechanical statements embedded in their design. In terms of broad aesthetics it's largely the same, since its chief problem was that it was naively copy-pasted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T18:37:04-07:00","id":104507,"title":"","content":"To me, the Dragonblooded represent the Exalted of Creation. Their numbers can be innumerable, their power is descended by blood, and their themes come from what currently are the pillars of Creation's stability, the 5 Immaculate/Elemental Dragons. They are the force, the mass of soldiers, healers, creators. They're the Exalted of the People. In the First Age they stood against the hordes of daeva and creatures fighting for the Primordials, ever spurred on by the glowing beacon of the Solars","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T18:41:56-07:00","id":104512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=104501#post104501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the 2e charmset only changed DB thematics in subtle and inadvertent ways, by messing up mechanical statements embedded in their design. In terms of broad aesthetics it's largely the same, since its chief problem was that it was naively copy-pasted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is. Hell, I hadn't noticed the changes to their mechanical statements until they begun to sprung up in this thread.<br /> <br /> Alot of the problems with 2e are damn subtle. It took my friends some time to come around as to WHY the 2e core gave me bad vibes, for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T11:43:34-07:00","id":104977,"title":"","content":"Second Edition was the successor to late First Edition.<br /> The cheap perfect defences were basically a response to the escalation caused by Sidereal Martial Arts and Deathlords.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T12:08:00-07:00","id":104994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102444#post102444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never got what the problem was with the five dragons being Gaia's five sub-souls. Surely it makes sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because then people use it to claim that they're not Exalted, but a type of devablooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T12:24:32-07:00","id":105007,"title":"","content":"People who think Dragon-Blooded are Fauxalted will continue to do so, whether the elemental dragons are Gaia's souls or children. The Dragon-Blooded are weaker, exalting as a dragon-blood means that you can't exalt as a celestial tier exalted, they have no divine mandate over Creation, and Gaia's children aren't Incarna, Yozi, or a Primordial.<br /> <br /> That said, the elemental dragons as children makes just as much sense as the elemental dragons as souls, and tends to fit in with Gaia actually being a mother.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T12:52:29-07:00","id":105025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=102444#post102444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never got what the problem was with the five dragons being Gaia's five sub-souls. Surely it makes sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that it's too pat.<br /> <br /> Exalted feels too solved. All the Yozis in Malfeas are the exact same type of being following the exact same clearly-established rules, and Autochthon and Gaia follow almost the exact same rules; every spirit is a god or demon or ghost, and they all have a set of unnecessarily-rigid definitions, etc.<br /> <br /> Those sorts of sweeping definitions don't improve the game; they make it feel smaller, narrower, less interesting. A writer tries to put a strange monster in and the audience is like &quot;oh it's just a third soul of zok, and the rules for it are...&quot; That doesn't feel deep or mysterious. The game needs more strange mysterious creatures, <i>especially</i> when it comes to things that are supposed to be epic and imposing, like ancient god-beings from the dawn of time.<br /> <br /> In fact, I think I'm gonna make another thread about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T17:32:08-07:00","id":105213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=104994#post104994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because then people use it to claim that they're not Exalted, but a type of devablooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whining of stupid internet posters doesn't seem a good reason to change the setting. And labels are irrelevant: they have the powers they have, whether you want to call them Exalts or not.<br /> <br /> But I do see Aquillion's point about how Exalted is too solved. Certainly by the end of second ed, everything was put into neat boxes, and lost some of its magic for me (though I think possibly this is just due to playing it for so long) and presumably other people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T07:27:32-07:00","id":105565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=105007#post105007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People who think Dragon-Blooded are Fauxalted will continue to do so, whether the elemental dragons are Gaia's souls or children. The Dragon-Blooded are weaker, exalting as a dragon-blood means that you can't exalt as a celestial tier exalted, <b>they have no divine mandate over Creation</b>, and Gaia's children aren't Incarna, Yozi, or a Primordial.<br /> <br /> That said, the elemental dragons as children makes just as much sense as the elemental dragons as souls, and tends to fit in with Gaia actually being a mother.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually the Exalted rulers of Creation have the Mandate of Heaven. You don't get to rule because you have the Mandate of Heaven, you get to hold the Mandate of Heaven because you're the ruler. Some 2e writers confused a divine mandate with the Divine Right of Kings, especially in the Yu-Shan direction book.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T08:52:15-07:00","id":105595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinjo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=105565#post105565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually the Exalted rulers of Creation have the Mandate of Heaven. You don't get to rule because you have the Mandate of Heaven, you get to hold the Mandate of Heaven because you're the ruler. Some 2e writers confused a divine mandate with the Divine Right of Kings, especially in the Yu-Shan direction book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted's Mandate of Heaven, at least in 2nd edition, is a thing that was specifically given to the Solar Exalted and is not just a marker that the current top dog holds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T09:41:47-07:00","id":105624,"title":"","content":"The whole EX3 team is excited to talk about our plans for Dragon-Blooded, but we have a bit of push left to do on the corebook. I will say this: there will be martial arts and Evocations that let Dragon-Blooded have more flashy elemental powers. We are also spicing up and broadening their Charm set. But do not expect them to have a basic element-bending power or 2e Infernal style designs, because that misses the point of the humanity present in the Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":20}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T09:54:09-07:00","id":105633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=105595#post105595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exalted's Mandate of Heaven, at least in 2nd edition, is a thing that was specifically given to the Solar Exalted and is not just a marker that the current top dog holds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, then, there's one other thing that could distinguish the Exalted Mandate from the Divine Right of Kings: is it revocable, or can it pass from group to group?<br /> <br /> The RL Mandate of Heaven was something that Chinese dynasties gained or lost based on how virtuous they were, supposedly. If multiple disasters struck during your reign, it could be said that you had lost the Mandate because of your misdeeds, and the gods were punishing the nation in general until you shaped up or got usurped. And then if the guy who killed you and took the throne did a better job, the Mandate was now theirs.<br /> <br /> The Divine Right, on the other hand, was said to be something integral to kingly bloodlines, and a king is a king no matter what he does. Whether they are virtuous people and whether they rule well or poorly is irrelevant - they still have the Right. Kings can fight Kings, but a bunch of lesser nobles can't rebel, kill the King, and then claim supreme rulership for themselves.<br /> <br /> Practical politics didn't follow the ideal, admittedly, but the concepts were pretty solid.<br /> <br /> Given the nature of Exaltation (power that cannot be taken away once it is given), I would think that the Solars ruling by Divine Right would be more consistent than Solars ruling by the Mandate of Heaven. It would also help to boost the Solar's status as &quot;returning kings&quot; rather than &quot;really powerful dudes who are possibly more worthy of being kings than the current guys&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T10:15:09-07:00","id":105643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=105633#post105633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Given the nature of Exaltation (power that cannot be taken away once it is given), I would think that the Solars ruling by Divine Right would be more consistent than Solars ruling by the Mandate of Heaven.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being unable to take away their Exaltation (bar the obvious route of, y'know, killing them) doesn't mean you can't take away their political power.<br /> <br /> Regardless of the fact that they're moving away from a portrayal consistent with Dreams of the First Age, look what happened with Merela.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would also help to boost the Solar's status as &quot;returning kings&quot; rather than &quot;really powerful dudes who are possibly more worthy of being kings than the current guys&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a status, it's a motif.<br /> <br /> Nobody is &quot;worthy&quot; of ruling anything based on the colour the magic inside them glows.<br /> <br /> In Exalted, if there's a Mandate of Heaven, it's more about Heaven's endorsement for Creation being ruled by humans. The rest is just details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T10:38:48-07:00","id":105648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=105633#post105633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, then, there's one other thing that could distinguish the Exalted Mandate from the Divine Right of Kings: is it revocable, or can it pass from group to group?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, it could. All it takes is the Unconquered Sun going &quot;Dragon-blooded are now the rulers of Creation&quot; and it would move. However, it hasn't happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T11:31:36-07:00","id":105678,"title":"","content":"The point is that the Exalted received the Mandate of Heaven by murdering the occupants of heaven. It has no more legitimacy to it than strength of arms being used to back it. Connotations to the real-life Mandate of Heaven notwithstanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T12:47:18-07:00","id":105759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=105678#post105678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is that the Exalted received the Mandate of Heaven by murdering the occupants of heaven. It has no more legitimacy to it than strength of arms being used to back it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, it <i>is</i> possible for groups that attain sovereign power through militant means to then sincerely incorporate the concept of rule of law.<br /> <br /> One could actually read whatever &quot;Mandate&quot; the Exalted were given over Creation as being a direct example of such procedures; an assurance that actions and relations between Heaven and Earth are based on cooperation and law, rather than the fear of force.<br /> <br /> Likewise, not all cases where social systems descend into disorder and violence are a proof that only the threat of force was holding them together. The circumstances are often more complicated than that, and are in Creation as well; that Yu-Shan did not back up the Shogunate probably had more to it than &quot;Terrestrial Exalted weren't strong enough to make the gods do what they wanted&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T13:04:53-07:00","id":105772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=104507#post104507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, the Dragonblooded represent the Exalted of Creation. Their numbers can be innumerable, their power is descended by blood, and their themes come from what currently are the pillars of Creation's stability, the 5 Immaculate/Elemental Dragons. They are the force, the mass of soldiers, healers, creators. They're the Exalted of the People. In the First Age they stood against the hordes of daeva and creatures fighting for the Primordials, ever spurred on by the glowing beacon of the Solars</div> </div> </div> </div>Iiiinteresting, because to me (and I'm a great Terrestrial fan), Sidereals are the Exalted of Creation. They, while arguably the most distanced and secluded of everyone, are actually tasked with keeping that mess of congealed Essence that is Creation running a few more days and they do so chiefly using Creation itself. Look at their Charms, and you'll find that a lot of them depend on the environment, utilizing the mechanics of the world with gods and elementals and stuff to their advantage.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I'd call Terrestrials Exalted of the People, either, because that's more Alchemicals to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T13:30:28-07:00","id":105789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=105759#post105759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, it <i>is</i> possible for groups that attain sovereign power through militant means to then sincerely incorporate the concept of rule of law.<br /> <br /> One could actually read whatever &quot;Mandate&quot; the Exalted were given over Creation as being a direct example of such procedures; an assurance that actions and relations between Heaven and Earth are based on cooperation and law, rather than the fear of force.<br /> <br /> Likewise, not all cases where social systems descend into disorder and violence are a proof that only the threat of force was holding them together. The circumstances are often more complicated than that, and are in Creation as well; that Yu-Shan did not back up the Shogunate probably had more to it than &quot;Terrestrial Exalted weren't strong enough to make the gods do what they wanted&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with every part of this. But that's taking us down a whole 'nother topic.<br /> <br /> [Creepy, derailing, time-lag edit]<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=105876#post105876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmmm...<br /> <br /> {looks out the window}<br /> <br /> Nope, factually incorrect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, here we go...<br /> <br /> 1) &quot;it <i>is</i> possible for groups that attain sovereign power through militant means to then sincerely incorporate the concept of rule of law&quot;<br /> <br /> Who's law?<br /> <br /> If I come to your house, take your things, commit violence upon your family and then say &quot;if you pay me protection money then I won't come again&quot; then I can sincerely commit myself to my word. I <i>want</i> your protection money. I am therefore best served by keeping my word. And if you pay me, then I will keep my word.<br /> <br /> But does that mean I'm committed to the rule of law? What about the rules that you were following before I came to your house? The law that said &quot;don't go into other people's houses, take their things and do violence upon them&quot;? Because I've taken a steaming dookie on <i>that</i> law. As it happens, I've committed myself not to any universal concept of &quot;rule of law&quot;, but to the rule of the laws that I have made myself,<br /> <br /> That's what the Normans did when they conquered England. No concern about Saxon law (which was actively, and very violently stamped out). But a strong dedication to Norman law. Hell, the Normans pretty much invented our modern English legal system.<br /> <br /> That's what the Europeans did when they conquered America. No concern for the local tribal laws or the native people. But a deep regard for their own law, Where it suited them. Little matters like not murdering your neighbor and payign fealty to your king still got casually tossed aside when it became inconvenient. And minor notes like not invading sovereign nations get disregarded to this day,<br /> <br /> That's what Russia is doing, as I type this, in Ukraine.<br /> <br /> And that's what happened in Exalted. The law of the Primordials was casually tossed aside and replaced (in theory) by the law of the Unconquered Sun. Except where the First Age Solars decided to imprison agents of heaven inside their Artifacts or to break the fabric of time itself or to steal worship away from their patron. I get that the First Age lore is going to change with E3, but Yu-Shen and the Deliberative have always been portrayed as committed to the laws that benefit them while ignoring the laws that inconvenience them. Just like every other nation on Earth.<br /> <br /> 2. &quot;One could actually read whatever &quot;Mandate&quot; the Exalted were given over Creation as being a direct example of such procedures; an assurance that actions and relations between Heaven and Earth are based on cooperation and law, rather than the fear of force.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm not saying you are wrong about this. But I still disagree.<br /> <br /> The Mandate was the Unconquered Sun saying &quot;take Creation, you earned it, go nuts. But leave Yu-Shen to us&quot;. It's Exalted's equivalent of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Munich_Agreement\" target=\"_blank\">Munich Agreement</a> - a bribe to lay down arms. The tone is 1at was different to 2nd, but when you look at the Gaes on the Mountain Folk and the departure of Autobot, you see a culture of fear in the First Age. Sidereals finally breaking into Lytek's office and wrestling him to the ground doesn't paint a picture of cooperation between Heaven and Earth. The resulting stagnation in the second age as heaven is left powerless without Iggy D or the Deliberative to guide them, also speaks of a tyrannical rule (not dissimilar to how the Realm is falling apart without Her Redness).<br /> <br /> The Mandate is an agreement signed over the bodies of the Primordials by their murderers. The Louisiana Purchase might have been a fair and legal document where France gave the USA dominion over its lands, but these were still lands stolen from the Native American Indians. But hey, who cares about the Indians? Because it's not like they are <b>strong</b> enough to contest the legality. The Mandate of Heaven is contingent on the Primordials (and the Lintha and the Dragon Kings) simply being too weak to contest that Creation shouldn't belong to the hairless monkeys who killed the architects of reality.<br /> <br /> 3. &quot;Likewise, not all cases where social systems descend into disorder and violence are a proof that only the threat of force was holding them together.&quot;<br /> <br /> Not proof, no. But these things do trend together. Remove an oppressive government from Somalia and oppressive terrorists fill the void. Have hurricane Katrina blow away the cops and watch the rioting begin. Have yourself an Arab Spring and suddenly the Ba'arth Party doesn't look quiet so unbeatable.<br /> <br /> Suffer for an indeterminate amount of time under the Primordials.... bur overthrow them once you are strong enough to over-power them.<br /> <br /> The Exalted didn't win because Truth and Justice were on their side (though, even DC's Superman isn't as close to Truth and Justice as Uncle Conqy is). The Exalted won because they had a bigger stick than the Primordials. They didn't win by calmly laying out how the rule of law will benefit all creatures great and small - from the Behemoth to the Field Mouse - they won through genocide and ganking fetich souls and then enforced a legal system that glorified themselves, protected their human stock and let the rest of Creations sentient (and sapient) beings go hang. And here's the crucial part <b>without</b> the protection that Primordal law had endowed them with.<br /> <br /> This is no different from the Mafia taking away the rights that your government grants you, but instead enforcing mafia law upon you. Or invading a nation because you don't like their system of government and you think your own system is superior (like Nazi Germany did in WW2 or the USA did in Iraq).<br /> <br /> 4. &quot;The circumstances are often more complicated than that,&quot;<br /> <br /> Are they? Now, I'm not saying that the Nazi invasion of Europe was the same as the First Gulf War or the Titanomancy. There are always circumstances and qualifiers, moral frameworks and mitigating circumstances. Murder is wrong, but if one murder will prevent ten murders then where is the greater evil?<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that the use of force is always wrong. And I'm not saying that it is <b>ever</b> right. I'm not making a moral judgement.I'm making a factual observation.<br /> <br /> The Exalted killed the Primordials and usurped their rule. Whether this is a just and right thing to do or not, is... not <i>irrelevant</i> as such but it is... not pertinent. They did it <b>because they could</b>. They used force. Fact. Successfully. Fact (outside of Gunstar). You can be Mafleas and attach the moral judgement that this is bad. You can be M-r-l and attach the moral judgement that this was good. But looking at the bear naked facts, the Exalted won through strength of arms. They were more powerful than the Primordials, so they got to make the law.<br /> <br /> The Roman's were more powerful than the nations they conquered, so they go to make the law. The Normans were more powerful than the Saxons, so they got to make the law. The American Secessionists were more powerful than the English oppressors, so they got to make the law. The Union was more powerful than the Confederacy so they got to outlaw slavery. Nazi Germany was more powerful than Poland so they got to gas the Jews.<br /> <br /> The circumstances that surround these events are all very different. The moral issues behind these events are also different. But what is <b>not</b> different, and where I disagree with you is where you think that the circumstances make a different. They do not. The strong make the law. End of story.<br /> <br /> 4. that Yu-Shan did not back up the Shogunate probably had more to it than &quot;Terrestrial Exalted weren't strong enough to make the gods do what they wanted&quot;.<br /> <br /> Yu-Shen (when it was ruled by the Primordials) did not back up humanity. Until the Solars were strong enough to bring about a revolution. The Mountain People did not want to provide the Deliberative with weapons. Until they were given no other choice. The Western Arbiter of Storms was not desperate to be horribly mutilated... but he was because the Solars were stronger than him.<br /> <br /> There are a myriad of complex reasons why Yu-Shan didn't back Dragon-Blooded rule of Creation. And these are touched upon through-out the Exalted game line. These reasons include Dragon-Blooded and Sidereal violence against the gods. And, were circumstances different, the Dragon-Blooded probably <i>could</i> have gained legitimate backing from heaven without resorting to force (I see a virtuous Terrestrial Circle making an impassioned case before the Unconquered Sun, explaining their case in detail and throwing the Dragon-Blooded host on his Mercy instead of inventing <i>Iris-Bulb Discourse</i> possibly swaying things). I am not denying the existence of compassion or saying that violence is the <b>only</b> way of getting things done. Because it's not. Violence is often a <i>terrible</i> way to achieve your goals (see the Arab Spring example I gave earlier).<br /> <br /> BUT..,<br /> <br /> The Solars casually violated heaven and they got away with it because of their vast powers. If the Dragon-Blooded had the power to best heaven (or casually mind-rape gods with Solar-Tier social charms) then things <i>would</i> be different.<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blooded's lack of personal power was not the only reason that Yu-Shan failed to back the Shogunate. (And slavery was not the only reason for the American Civil War.) But if the Dragon-Blooded had been more powerful then they would have been able to force cooperation (whether through coercion or by killing all the gods and giving Yu-Shan to a faction more biddable - which is exactly what the Solars did to earn the Mandate of Heaven in the first instance.)<br /> <br /> 5. &quot;{looks out the window}<br /> <br /> Nope, factually incorrect&quot;<br /> <br /> Really? You follow Native American law and America doesn't invade sovereign nations? You don't have presidents like Nixon and Clinton who flaunt the laws of your own nation? You don't have criminals who break the rule of law because they can? You are the citizen of a nation that enforces the law <i>without</i> using physical violence to put people into cages or to kill them with lethal injections?<br /> <br /> Or do you perhaps see another country when you look out of the window?<br /> <br /> Whenever a policeman uses a taser, or pepperspray, or a gun, or self-defense training to take a purp into custody they are using physical force. Whenever a criminal comes in peacefully to avoid getting tazed or wrestled to the ground then law enforcement is using the threat of force. Every guard on the prison wall is, at least, using coercion to keep the criminals in the pen. And the criminals stay imprisoned because they are not strong enough to break out.<br /> <br /> I am not attaching a moral judgement to law enforcement. I don't think anyone would want to live in a world where murderers and rapists do as they please. But what keeps the scum off the streets is <b>force</b>. You can dress it up in a pretty blue uniform and have men in wigs write down what kinds of force are acceptable on rolls of dusty parchment but the fact is that violence and threat of violence is what gets the job done.<br /> <br /> The law is self-serving. The law of my nation tells me I have to pay tax, and what plants I can eat, and whom I must pay to take a car on the road and what digital media I'm allowed to copy. These are not universal tenants of justice handed down on stone tablets by a creator as &quot;The Rule of Law&quot;, but the edicts of men trying to run a nation.Attach whatever moral rational you want to that. I, for one, would rather a democratic government apply the threat of force to me than a gang of pirates or a cooperation.<br /> <br /> But Exalted doesn't even have that. They discarded The Rule of Law that really was passed on down by the Creator, and what they replaced it with was not a democratic republic but a military theocracy. If Al Queida took control of the USA tomorrow and enforced Sharia Law would that be the tyrannical actions of might makes right or the &quot;sincere incorporation of the concept of rule of law&quot;? I leave that one to the reader's own judgements.<br /> <br /> I may be morally incorrect, but you sir, are the one who is &quot;factually incorrect&quot;. The facts are that might makes the law. Whether this is good or bad remains subjective but I don't think you'll find many Lintha who think overthrowing the Primordials was right or many Solar's who think that of the Usurpation.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-06-2014, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T13:59:18-07:00","id":105808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=105648#post105648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically, it could. All it takes is the Unconquered Sun going &quot;Dragon-blooded are now the rulers of Creation&quot; and it would move. However, it hasn't happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather, <i>you don't know if it has happened</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T14:53:09-07:00","id":105845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=105772#post105772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iiiinteresting, because to me (and I'm a great Terrestrial fan), Sidereals are the Exalted of Creation. They, while arguably the most distanced and secluded of everyone, are actually tasked with keeping that mess of congealed Essence that is Creation running a few more days and they do so chiefly using Creation itself. Look at their Charms, and you'll find that a lot of them depend on the environment, utilizing the mechanics of the world with gods and elementals and stuff to their advantage.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I'd call Terrestrials Exalted of the People, either, because that's more Alchemicals to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sidereals are the Exalted of Heaven, and as such are tasked with the machinations of Heaven. Yu-shan is the seat of the Gods, former seat of the Primordials, and is the house of Fate. Theirs is the work of fates, divine plans and mandates, and the protection of Heaven and it's purview from without. In a way, they take the roles of mythological angels combined with secret agents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T15:40:02-07:00","id":105876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=105789#post105789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree with every part of this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm...<br /> <br /> {looks out the window}<br /> <br /> Nope, factually incorrect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T15:47:18-07:00","id":105879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=105845#post105845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sidereals are the Exalted of Heaven, and as such are tasked with the machinations of Heaven.</div> </div> </div> </div>'We are the truth of the world, Creation is but a projection of its real heart, and all of it exists at the whims of its Gods and Elemental puppetmasters' is the Sidereal view, and should be only the Sidereal view, challenged by the other splats and the importance of Creation itself on the ground, and how for them and it is all just resources or nuisances. Somehow, that became the view of the entire setting since Sidereals first came out, though... I suppose it tickled the fancy of even the writers to be writing about the 'truth' of Creation, or the idea of Sidereals sitting at the comfortable core of the world and directing all the rest of it, perhaps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T10:13:31-07:00","id":106362,"title":"","content":"To clarify my earlier post: I am a post-structuralist thinker. I do not believe in the individual. I do not believe in autonomy. We are all subjects, constructs of the ideological state apparatus (ISA). I apply very humanist sentiments to Exalted. Exalted is a safe (and productive) place to uphold these ideals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T10:29:47-07:00","id":106370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=106362#post106362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify my earlier post: I am a post-structuralist thinker. I do not believe in the individual. I do not believe in autonomy. We are all subjects, constructs of the ideological state apparatus (ISA). I apply very humanist sentiments to Exalted. Exalted is a safe (and productive) place to uphold these ideals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this an appropriate page for researching the concept you mention?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.marxists.org/reference/archive/althusser/1970/ideology.htm\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.marxists.org/reference/archive/althusser/1970/ideology.htm\" target=\"_blank\"> Ideology and Ideological State Apparatuses by Louis Althusser 1969-70 </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.marxists.org/reference/archive/althusser/1970/ideology.htm\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.marxists.org/reference/archive/althusser/1970/ideology.htm </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T12:49:15-07:00","id":106454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=106362#post106362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are all subjects, constructs of the ideological state apparatus (ISA).</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't keep all these Exalted acronyms straight.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T13:31:41-07:00","id":106484,"title":"","content":"...What earlier post? Is there a post I can't see to which post-structuralism is somehow a clarification?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T15:53:40-07:00","id":106574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't feel like that CLARIFIED much of anything</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't understand it even after reading that essay on Ideological Society Apparatuses. Maybe if I looked up &quot;humanist&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T16:21:03-07:00","id":106602,"title":"","content":"&quot;As Marx said, every child knows that a social formation which did not reproduce the conditions of production at the same time as it produced would not last a year.&quot;<br /> <br /> I wonder if Marx ever had a conversation with a child.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T16:54:27-07:00","id":106613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=106602#post106602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;As Marx said, every child knows that a social formation which did not reproduce the conditions of production at the same time as it produced would not last a year.&quot;<br /> <br /> I wonder if Marx ever had a conversation with a child.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would hope Marx would use plainer language, if so. Such as &quot;a woodsman has to do more than cut down trees to maintain his living; he also has to sharpen his axe-head when it dulls, or replace the haft when it breaks. Not to mention spend some of his profit on shelter and food for himself, so that he can survive to continue working.&quot;<br /> <br /> The essay is long on extremely abstract, generalized language and short on accessible, illustrative examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-05-2014, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T08:10:01-07:00","id":106898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=106613#post106613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The essay is long on extremely abstract, generalized language and short on accessible, illustrative examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome to continental philosophy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/832-surlyseraph","name":"SurlySeraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T08:29:44-07:00","id":106911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=106362#post106362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am a post-structuralist thinker.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is absolutely the most horrifying thing I have heard from any of the 3rd ed development team.<br /> <br /> Though post-structuralism does at least avoid all those very long arguments about the precise meaning of words which crop up on this forum a fair bit. So, so many arguments I've seen where I've just thought &quot;guys! Post-structuralism! All your arguments about what exactly words mean are meaningless!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T10:14:27-07:00","id":106956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/102106-explain-the-dragonblooded-design-paradigm-to-me?p=105772#post105772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I'd call Terrestrials Exalted of the People, either, because that's more Alchemicals to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alchemicals are the Exalts of the people in the sense of being &quot;made for&quot; and &quot;serving&quot; the people, Solars in terms of being &quot;from&quot; the people and remaining clearly human, Dragonblooded in the sense of being &quot;like&quot; the power of the masses.<br /> <br /> Terrestrials are about rough, unrefined, lowly, plentiful power that comes together and becomes much more than its parts are as individuals, by working together as a people. Elements coming together in harmony is a great symbol for this idea of &quot;low&quot; but plentiful power that works together to be something greater. The power of the masses.<br /> <br /> (They're also positioned as aristocrats, I think, just to show that because your power is like the power of the masses is, realistically, no guarantee that you'll be particularly selfless towards the masses!)<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded as soldier Exalts is really more of a spin off of them expressing mass power, more than it is a limitation or focus to them. (Soldiers are part of an mass army, usually for a state or a culture or a people, while warriors aren't necessarily.)<br /> <br /> I think this kind of power seems actually really hard to actually express through Charms though, which are to a degree personalised and individualistic expressions of flair and heroism, which might be why a lot of Terrestrial Charms don't really seek to embody it there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}